  "final_message": "To comply with **ARCH-4** (published event changes must be additive to prevent breaking deployed consumers such as `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`), `OrderPlaced` now retains `placedAt` and `totalCents` as deprecated fields alongside the newly introduced `createdAt` and `amountCents`.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n- **[`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L32)** and **[`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L45-L67)**:\n  - Added `createdAt` and `amountCents` to match Payments and Customer API conventions.\n  - Kept `placedAt` and `totalCents` populated for backward compatibility with downstream consumers.\n- **[app.test.ts](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/orders-service/test/app.test.ts#L21-L34)** & **[adapters.test.ts](file:///C:/avg/w3/r/orders-service/test/adapters.test.ts#L46-L55)**:\n  - Updated test assertions to verify that both the new fields and backward-compatible fields are present and correctly populated.\n\n### Verification\n- `npm test`: All 39 unit and integration tests passing.\n- `npm run arch`: All dependency cruiser architecture checks passing.\n- `npm run typecheck`: Passed with 0 TypeScript diagnostics.\n",
